The self-check runs on every interrupt of the timer, traced or not,
so the one walk the loop check takes on trust is on the timer's path.
It checks the same, so only the loop check's guard on the cut catches it.

Caught-by: loop-bounds
Witness: loop-bounds

diff --git a/kernel/timer.c b/kernel/timer.c
--- a/kernel/timer.c
+++ b/kernel/timer.c
@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@ bool timer_trap_enter(bool pending)
 {
     bool traced = debug_trace;
     if (!traced && pending) {
+        selfcheck_run();
         sched_time(counter_read());
     }
     return traced;
